<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78434" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραμπ-έχω</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραμπ-ίσχω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cover
				with a cloak</i> or <i>robe</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν τοῦ σώματος αἰσχύνην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alcid.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1406a29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>wrap</i> a thing <i>round as a cloak</i> or <i>disguise</i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραμπίσχειν</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έχειν</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> λόγους</span>
			<i>use a cloak of</i> words, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				282
			</span></i> :—
				Med.
			, <i>allege as a pretext</i>, c. acc., <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.Sacr.</u>
				1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
